<?xml version="1.0" ?>

<!--
====================================================================
= SBND-only CV / error band, matched to the injected parameter scan =
====================================================================

Purpose: produce the SBND central value and its systematic error band in the
SAME 1D reconstructed-energy bins, and at the SAME exposure, as the injected
grid points under parameter_scan/. That band is what
plotting/sbnd_data_access.ipynb compares each injected point against when
counting how many bins fall outside it.

Derived from xml/contours/contours_sbnd2d.xml, which stays the config of record
for the contours. Three deliberate differences:

1. SBND ONLY. The scan comparison never touches ICARUS, and ICARUS is still
   blinded, so its channels, MC files, detector systematics and the
   shape-blind norm entry are all absent here. Only SBND remains, so the
   detector-folded-into-channel trick that contours_sbnd2d.xml needs is kept
   purely for name compatibility (see below) rather than out of necessity.

2. var0 IS 1D RecoE, not the 2D RecoE;pn. The contours fit in 2D, but the scan
   files are 1D in reconstructed energy, and PROfit writes an error band only
   for variables flagged for plotting. Making RecoE var0 puts the band in
   ErrorBand/Var0 with no plot-flag games, and keeps true L/E at var1 where
   the numudis model expects it (variable_index="1").

   The bin edges below are byte-identical to the scan files: 16 bins
   0.3-1.5 GeV for ccqelike, 14 bins 0.4-2.0 GeV for nproton.

3. THE SBND POT IS THE SCAN'S EXPOSURE, NOT THE DEV SAMPLE'S. See below.

NAMES ARE DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED from contours_sbnd2d.xml: one detector "SBN"
with the detector folded into the channel names (sbndccqelike / sbndnproton),
giving fullnames like nu_SBN_sbndccqelike_target. Every apply_to_subchannel
and norm pattern in the variation_list is a CASE-SENSITIVE regex matched
against those fullnames, and they match on the lowercase "sbnd" inside the
CHANNEL name. Renaming the detector to "SBND" and the channels to plain
"ccqelike"/"nproton" would leave no lowercase "sbnd" to match: the hist1d
entries would abort the run (a non-matching apply_to_subchannel is fatal) and
the CORSIKA norm would quietly stop applying. Keeping the names also means the
error-band keys here are the same ones contours_sbndunblind produces.

EXPOSURE. The scan files carry no record of the POT they assumed, so it was
reverse-engineered from their rates against this same MC:

    SBND ccqelike   4235.7 events  /  100239.9 at 1e20  ->  4.226e18
    SBND nproton    1290.5 events  /   30271.9 at 1e20  ->  4.263e18

Those two agree to 0.9%, which is what makes this a pure exposure difference
rather than a selection-efficiency one - an efficiency change would not land
on both channels at the same ratio. And that ~4.2e18 is not a coincidence: it
is the actual collected SBND data POT, 4.196270e+18, already used by every
xml/coverage/*.xml in this repo. So the scan was run at the real collected
exposure, and this config uses that documented number rather than the
reverse-engineered 4.234e18 it agrees with to within 1%.

The residual ~1% is the scan's MC version against ours and is expected; the
notebook's comparison should check that ratio and complain if it ever drifts
far from unity.

NOTE this is NOT the 5e18 that jobs/contours/contours_sbndunblind.ini scales
to (1e20 x `scale = sbnd 0.05`), which is about 19% higher - that config
targets a round dev-sample number, this one reproduces the scan. Changing the
pot below requires a fresh `process`: POT is folded into the event weights at
process time, cannot be patched at plot time, and forcing past the cache check
would silently give wrong normalization.
-->

<mode name="nu" />

<!--
One detector, as in contours_sbnd2d.xml. The name "SBN" rather than "SBND" is
name compatibility, not physics: the baseline enters through true_baseline in
the L/E expression, never through the detector name.

The POT is the collected SBND data exposure (as in xml/coverage/*.xml), which
is what the scan was generated at - NOT the 1e20 nominal.
-->
<detector name="SBN" pot="4.196270e+18" />

<!--
Two-flavour nu_mu disappearance, unchanged from contours_sbnd2d.xml. The L/E
parameter reads variable_index="1", which is why true L/E stays var1 in every
channel below.
-->
<model tag="numudis">
    <rule index="0" name="No Osc"/>
    <rule index="1" name="Numu Dis"/>
    <parameter name="L/E" variable_index="1"/>
</model>

<!--
==================================
= Exclusive final-state analysis =
==================================
Two channels split by reconstructed proton multiplicity:
 - ccqelike: exactly one reconstructed proton
 - nproton:  more than one reconstructed proton

var0 is the fit/plot variable (1D RecoE, matching the scan bin-for-bin), var1
the true L/E the model oscillates in, var2 true energy for the cross-section
splines (binning="var2" in the variation_list). var1 and var2 are plot="false"
- PROfit indexes those flags by variable number off the FIRST channel, so the
flags on sbndccqelike are the ones that decide what lands in ErrorBand/.
-->
<channel name="sbndccqelike" unit="Reconstructed Neutrino Energy [GeV]">

    <bins unit="RecoE" edges="0.3 0.4 0.46 0.52 0.58 0.64 0.7 0.76 0.82 0.88 0.94 1.0 1.06 1.13 1.2 1.3 1.5"/>
    <bins unit="True L/E"     min="0.0" max="3.0" nbins="300" plot="false"/>
    <bins unit="True E [GeV]" min="0.3" max="3.0" nbins="20"  plot="false"/>

    <subchannel name="intime"  plotname="Intime Cosmics" color="#FBBC04"/>
    <subchannel name="cos"     plotname="Cosmics"        color="#E37400"/>
    <subchannel name="nc"      plotname="NC"             color="#FF6961"/>
    <subchannel name="nuecc"   plotname="#nu_e CC"       color="#47ffed"/>
    <subchannel name="othercc" plotname="Other #nu CC"   color="#03fc3d"/>
    <subchannel name="target"  plotname="Target"         color="#99CCFF"/>

</channel>

<channel name="sbndnproton" unit="Reconstructed Neutrino Energy [GeV]">

    <bins unit="RecoE" edges="0.4 0.5 0.59 0.67 0.75 0.83 0.91 0.99 1.07 1.16 1.26 1.37 1.5 1.7 2.0"/>
    <bins unit="True L/E"     min="0.0" max="3.0" nbins="300" plot="false"/>
    <bins unit="True E [GeV]" min="0.3" max="3.0" nbins="20"  plot="false"/>

    <subchannel name="intime"  plotname="Intime Cosmics" color="#FBBC04"/>
    <subchannel name="cos"     plotname="Cosmics"        color="#E37400"/>
    <subchannel name="nc"      plotname="NC"             color="#FF6961"/>
    <subchannel name="nuecc"   plotname="#nu_e CC"       color="#47ffed"/>
    <subchannel name="othercc" plotname="Other #nu CC"   color="#03fc3d"/>
    <subchannel name="target"  plotname="Target"         color="#99CCFF"/>

</channel>



<!--
Declare the histogram-based detector systematics. SBND sections only; the
ICARUS Run 2 / Run 4 sections from contours_sbnd2d.xml are gone with their
channels.
-->
<HistVarFiles>

    <!-- Gain Variation -->
    <HistVarSection name="Gain_sbnd_Run1">
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="GainHigh_sbnd_Run1" knobval="-2.5"/>
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="GainLow_sbnd_Run1" knobval="2.5"/>
    </HistVarSection>

    <!-- SCE: Space Charge Effect -->
    <HistVarSection name="SCE_sbnd_Run1">
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="SCE0x_sbnd_Run1" knobval="-1"/>
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="SCE2x_sbnd_Run1" knobval="1"/>
    </HistVarSection>

    <!-- Trigger Emulation -->
    <HistVarSection name="TriggerEmulation_sbnd_Run1">
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="TriggerEmulationM1_sbnd_run1" knobval="-1"/>
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="TriggerEmulationP1_sbnd_run1" knobval="1"/>
    </HistVarSection>

    <!-- Toroid Calibration -->
    <HistVarSection name="ToroidCalibration_sbnd_Run1">
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="ToroidCalibration_generic_RunX" knobval="1"/>
    </HistVarSection>

    <!-- Protons Missing the Target -->
    <HistVarSection name="ProtonMiss_sbnd_Run1">
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="ProtonMissLow_generic_RunX" knobval="-1"/>
        <variation filename="work/detsys_main.root" histname="ProtonMissHigh_generic_RunX" knobval="1"/>
    </HistVarSection>

</HistVarFiles>

<variation_list>

    <!--
    Here we configure statistical uncertainties. These are Poissonian
    uncertainties due to the finite number of MC (or off-beam data) signal
    candidates in each bin. This should always be included.
    -->
    <allowlist type="mcstat" plotname="MC Stats" tag="stat,MC Stats">mcstat</allowlist>
    
    <!--
    Interaction Model Systematics (AR23+ Interaction Model)
    -->

