    <!--
    Here we configure flux systematics. These correspond to uncertainties in
    the neutrino flux prediction, which comes from a variety of sources.
    Broadly, we have two major categories of flux systematics:
        - Hadron production systematics: these correspond to uncertainties in
        hadron production cross sections, which affect how many pions and kaons
        are produced in the target and hence how many neutrinos are produced from
        their decays.
        - Beamline systematics: these correspond to uncertainties in the beamline
        configuration, such as the horn current and skin depth of the current in
        the horn. These affect how the hadrons are focused and hence the
        resulting neutrino flux.
